{"code":"properties","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" holds"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"$process_person_profile: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so PostHog makes no person profile, and "},{"code":"$geoip_disable: true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so PostHog doesn’t add a location from the request’s IP address. A record with no session (one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tracked by a tracker without "},{"code":"Enricher.sessions()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") is its own anonymous person, linked to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing: PostHog rejects a whole batch when one of its events has no "},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A record a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store recovers after a relaunch keeps its session, so it goes out under the "},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"$session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" of its first send. PostHog counts a person per "},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so its unique users"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are sessions. The session is also sent as "},{"code":"$session_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which PostHog’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sessions and web analytics group events by ("},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the UUIDv7 they require); a record"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with no session has none. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context, and any other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context value, aren’t sent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"code":"plan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"code":"PropertyReader","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, an element of an array is "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is "},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"property whose name starts with "},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which only a hand-written "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write, or is "},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", is left out and logged at notice level, as PostHog reads those"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names as settings ("},{"code":"$set","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"$process_person_profile","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") or the identity."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"},{"type":"text","text":" also holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for:"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Key","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_namespace"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_version"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_build"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The bundle identifier, version and build, each left out when "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_model"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_type"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"DeviceKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The model, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mobile"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tablet"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Desktop"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TV"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vision"},{"type":"text","text":" for the form factor; no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_type"},{"type":"text","text":" for a watch"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$locale","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LocaleKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as ","type":"text"},{"code":"en-US","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$network_wifi","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"$network_cellular","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NetworkKey"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Whether the connection is Wi-Fi, and whether it is cellular","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"$os_name","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$os_version","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"OperatingSystemKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The operating system’s name and version"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out of the request, and the batch’s other records are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: one whose event and version "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":" doesn’t describe, one whose event name starts with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a name PostHog keeps for its own events), one whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one that holds a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form, and one too large for PostHog to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":")."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns them as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":"s, which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" logs and reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" splits a batch into requests within the encoder’s limit, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PostHogEncoding\/documentation\/PostHogEncoding\/PostHogBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"tex